# What goes into an image is what the public snapshot contains (.publish-exclude)
# and nothing more, wherever the image is built: from this repository or from
# the public one. spec/lib/dockerignore_spec.rb holds the two files together.
# rsync matches a pattern without "/" at any depth, Docker only at the root;
# such patterns are therefore also written with "**/" here.

# Version control, CI and the mirror's own files
.git
**/.git
.github
**/.github
.publish-exclude
**/.publish-exclude
.publish-overlay
**/.publish-overlay

# Licensed standards: never in an image
docs/*.pdf
docs/*.PDF
**/*.pdf
**/*.PDF

# Internal working documents
docs/operations
docs/HackMD_260812.md
docs/Prompts_Datenintermediaer_260812.md
docs/pod-dpp_Vorschlag.md
docs/Walkthrough_Pod_VarianteB.md
docs/Guide.md
docs/Walkthrough_DID_Intermediaer.md
docs/Walkthrough-Delegation.md
docs/CarrierRedesign.md

# Cluster and operations: internal hosts, secret names, measurement scripts
k8s
**/k8s
script
**/script
docs/CarrierMigrationRunbook.md
docs/verification/PACE-Kommandos.md
docs/verification/PROTOKOLL.md

# Host-local gems and bundler config never leak into the image
.bundle
**/.bundle
vendor/bundle

# Runtime, local data, dev and test artefacts
log
**/log
tmp
**/tmp
storage
**/storage
**/*.log
**/*.sqlite3
**/*.sqlite3-*
spec
.rspec
README.md
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
**/.DS_Store

# Secrets: never baked into an image
**/*.enc
**/*_revocation.json
**/*.env
**/.env
**/.env.*
config/master.key
config/credentials/*.key
